								<em>Machine Party</em> is an odd game for me. Having never played a proper ‘party’ game before (like Mario Party), I went in quite excited to see what these games were all about. All I can say is this game was well… nothing special? <br><br>The time I had on this game was so bittersweet due to its highly repetitive nature and short playtime, however the minigames were overall very fun. Certain minigames definitely felt less polished and less thought-out (looking at you Spine Breaker!), but the games where you were able to push the other players were definitely the highlight. I keep reliving the memory of stunlocking one of my friends into a corner on Stable Footing and hearing him cuss me out as he fell.<br><br>However, this is one of those games where it is <em>highly</em> dependent on who you play with. I played with a group of friends with a great sense of humour and the ability to <em>actually</em> make the most of the minigames, which definitely made my experience better. In saying this, it was felt towards the end of our consecutive runs that we were running out of things to do and were quickly getting bored. If further minigames were added to pad out the runtime a bit, and true randomisation was implemented for the order of the minigames, the longevity could definitely increase my opinion of this game. However, I’m not sure how likely that will be unfortunately.<br><br>Because of the lack of replayability, <em>Machine Party</em> sits at the middle of the road, 5/10, for me.
							</div>
